<!--
  ComboboxCreatableDemo.rozie — content-STABLE create-row screenshot fixture for
  the pure-Rozie Combobox `creatable` mode (Phase 86 R3, plan 86-06).

  The one thing no happy-dom mount-and-drive behavioral test
  (creatable.behavior.test.ts) can prove: the create row's real on-screen
  appearance, and that it renders LAST, visibly after every real option, in
  the same frame. This demo exists ONLY to make that a deterministic pixel
  cell — never extend it for behavior (mirrors ComboboxMultiDemo.rozie /
  ComboboxFloatingDemo.rozie's own "never bolt behavior onto the screenshot
  cell" discipline).

  Made deterministic by:
    1. `creatable` set with a FIXED query ("kiwi") seeded via the composed
       Combobox's own `seedQuery` handle — a query that matches NO option in
       the four-item fruit list, so the create row is the sole trailing
       affordance below all four rendered options (a deterministic frame
       showing options + the create row together, in one screenshot).
    2. The popup is opened DETERMINISTICALLY at mount via the composed
       Combobox's own `focus` handle — `$refs.creatableCombobox.focus()`,
       deferred one macrotask (setTimeout(0)) past `$onMount`, mirroring
       ComboboxMultiDemo.rozie's identical child-ref-readiness workaround (a
       child's $expose handle is not yet registered when a PARENT's
       $onMount runs synchronously on Solid). `seedQuery('kiwi')` is called
       BEFORE `focus()`, not after: Combobox's own `onFocus` handler runs
       `e.target.select()` on every real focus event, and on Solid
       specifically (only) the R2 `openingInProgress` reentrancy guard's
       deferred microtask re-focus fires a SECOND native focus event once the
       anchor's DOM is recreated (see Combobox.rozie's onFocus doc comment) —
       re-running `select()` again. Seeding first means BOTH the first
       (all six targets) and Solid's second `select()` call land on the
       SAME already-seeded text, so every target's baseline shows the
       identical browser text-selection highlight instead of Solid alone
       diffing by a re-selected-after-the-fact highlight discovered during
       this plan's own VR run (see the SUMMARY's Deviations).
    3. An explicit `height` on the root box (not auto-sized from flow
       content) — mirrors ComboboxMultiDemo.rozie's point 3: the popup's
       `position: absolute` panel does not grow an ancestor's auto height,
       so without an explicit height tall enough for the input + the
       four-option + create-row open popup, the popup would render OUTSIDE
       `[data-testid="rozie-mount"]`'s captured bounding box and never be
       captured.
    4. A DISTINCT idBase so the aria ids never collide with any other
       combobox cell.

  One .rozie source compiles to six per-framework screenshot consumers; the
  Linux PNG baseline is generated separately in pinned Linux Docker (NOT here
  — feedback_vr_linux_baselines). Until it lands the matrix cell auto-fixmes
  on `baselineExists()`.
-->

<rozie name="ComboboxCreatableDemo">

<components>
{
  Combobox: '../../packages/ui/combobox/src/Combobox.rozie',
}
</components>

<data>
{
  value: null,
}
</data>

<script>
const OPTIONS = [
  { value: 'apple', label: 'Apple' },
  { value: 'banana', label: 'Banana' },
  { value: 'cherry', label: 'Cherry' },
  { value: 'date', label: 'Date' },
]

// See the header comment (point 2) for why this is deferred one macrotask
// past $onMount rather than called synchronously.
$onMount(() => {
  setTimeout(() => {
    // Seed BEFORE focus — see the header comment (point 2) for why the order
    // matters (a Solid-only reentrancy re-select discovered via this plan's
    // own VR run).
    $refs.creatableCombobox.seedQuery('kiwi')
    $refs.creatableCombobox.focus()
  }, 0)
})
</script>

<template>
<div class="combobox-creatable-demo">
  <Combobox
    ref="creatableCombobox"
    r-model:value="$data.value"
    :options="OPTIONS"
    creatable
    placeholder="Search fruit…"
    ariaLabel="Fruit (creatable)"
    idBase="creatable-combobox"
  />
</div>
</template>

<style>
.combobox-creatable-demo {
  box-sizing: border-box;
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  width: 360px;
  height: 380px;
  padding: 1rem;
}
/* Combobox's own onFocus() calls e.target.select() on every real focus event
   (existing, documented select-all-on-focus UX, unrelated to this fixture).
   On Solid ONLY, the R2 openingInProgress reentrancy guard's deferred
   microtask re-focus (see Combobox.rozie's onFocus doc comment) may fire a
   SECOND native focus event after this demo's own seedQuery()+focus() pair
   settles — non-deterministically leaving the input's text selected or not
   by the time Playwright captures the screenshot (discovered as a genuine
   cross-run flake while proving this cell in Docker: the SAME build failed
   0/3 then 3/3 retries on [solid] alone). Neutralizing the browser's default
   text-selection highlight makes the selected and unselected renders
   pixel-identical, so this SPECIFIC race can never show up as a VR diff
   again. `.rozie-combobox-input` is rendered by the COMPOSED Combobox child,
   not this demo's own scoped markup, so a plain scoped rule's
   [data-rozie-s-*] attribute never matches it — the engine-DOM `:root { }`
   escape hatch (Phase 34) is required, host-qualified by
   `.combobox-creatable-demo` so it stays scoped to this one fixture. A
   fixture-local fix, not a Combobox.rozie change — the select-all-on-focus
   behavior itself is untouched and still fires. */
:root {
  .combobox-creatable-demo .rozie-combobox-input::selection {
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
  }
}
</style>

</rozie>
